"""Engine fixtures for Forkluck Recipes for Mac, generated by the real engines.

The Mac app ports the normalized costing engine (`domains/recipes/health.py`),
the nutrition rollup (`domains/recipes/nutrition.py`), `purchase_quantity`,
the FoodData Central adapter, the allergen hint parser and catalog activation
to Swift. Each test here runs the Python original over fixed inputs and pins
what it answers in `forkluck/parity/*.json`, which the Mac repository copies
into its test bundle and asserts its ports against.

Costing and nutrition read hand-authored scenarios from
`forkluck/parity/scenarios/`, in the engine-input shape the Mac snapshots
decode (keys are human slugs, never database ids). Every fixture records the
command that regenerates it:

    cd apps/api && UPDATE_ENGINE_FIXTURE=1 .venv/bin/python manage.py test forkluck.test_mac_parity_fixtures

Without the variable a missing file is written and an existing one is
asserted equal, so a change to an engine fails here until the fixture is
regenerated and copied across.
"""

